  "theorem_boundary": {
    "general_composition": "under a pointwise union of component nulls, the minimum of independently fixed component e-factors is dominated by the factor associated with whichever null is active",
    "not_covered": "outcome-dependent factor-grid redesign, unregistered candidate or fallback changes, physical safety, or real-world validity",
    "parameter_mixture": "an outcome-independent mixture over fixed component-parameter tuples preserves the e-process property",
    "relation_to_v3": "version 3 is the shared-fraction diagonal restriction after expressing the Bernoulli factor as a linear harm-score factor",
    "time_product": "products remain test supermartingales even when the active component changes arbitrarily with the past"
